# Commit messages

When writing a commit message, follow
[How to Write a Git Commit Message](https://cbea.ms/git-commit/).

1. Separate the subject from the body with a blank line.
2. Limit the subject to 50 characters (72 is the hard limit).
3. Capitalize the subject line.
4. Do not end the subject with a period.
5. Use the imperative mood in the subject. It must complete: "If applied, this commit will …".
6. Wrap the body at 72 characters.
7. Use the body to explain what and why, not how. Omit the body only when the subject is enough.

```
Add a first-time setup section to the README

A fresh clone has no SSH key or console password, and the board
is not yet running this image. Spell out that path so the first
flash is the SD WIC, not an A/B update.
```
